  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;Values are a measure of basicity. Higher the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;value, greater will be basicity.<br /><br />(I) Basic character &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi><mtext>&#8201;s-&#8201;character</mtext></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> has more % s-character than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> so it is less basic as compare to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> Hence <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br /><br />(II) In the (ii) structure lone pair present on the N atom is involved in aromaticity so, it is difficult to donate. Hence, least basic<br /><br />Thus, the correct order will be: <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></p>"
